{
  "_comment": "Golden vectors for the recurrence engine. The engine is civil (wall-clock): each vector gives `anchor`/`from`/`expected` both as Unix ms and as the wall-clock time they show in `tz` (`*_local`, ISO without offset). The test runs nextOccurrence(rule, anchor, from, tz) on the instants and the civil engine on the locals. `expected` is null when the rule is invalid or the next occurrence falls outside the JS Date range (|ms| > 8.64e15); `expected_local` is null only when the rule is invalid. `parse` lists rules the parser must accept or reject. Asserted by packages/shared/src/recurrence.test.ts.",
  "vectors": [
    {
      "name": "daily every 1, on schedule",
      "rule": "FREQ=DAILY",
      "tz": "UTC",
      "anchor": 1672531200000,
      "anchor_local": "2023-01-01T00:00:00",
      "from": 1672531200000,
      "from_local": "2023-01-01T00:00:00",
      "expected": 1672617600000,
      "expected_local": "2023-01-02T00:00:00"
    },
